{"name":"Ramsons","hex":"#195456","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ramsons","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wild relative of chives, of species Allium ursinum, having edible leaves and roots."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ramsons"}],"entries":[{"title":"Allium ursinum","blocks":[{"text":"Allium ursinum, known as wild garlic, ramsons, cowleekes, cows's leek, cowleek, buckrams, broad-leaved garlic, wood garlic, bear leek, Eurasian wild garlic, onion grass, or bear's garlic, is a bulbous perennial flowering plant in the amaryllis family, Amaryllidaceae. It is native to Eurasia, where it grows in moist woodland. It is a wild relative of onion and garlic, all belonging to the same genus, Allium. There are two recognized subspecies: A. ursinum subsp. ursinum and A. ursinum subsp. ucrainicum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Photo_of_Allium_Ursinum%2C_wild_garlic%2C_north-west_Hampshire%2C_UK%2C_May_2014.jpg/330px-Photo_of_Allium_Ursinum%2C_wild_garlic%2C_north-west_Hampshire%2C_UK%2C_May_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allium_ursinum","wikidata":"Q130882"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/387_Allium_ursinum.jpg/330px-387_Allium_ursinum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/387_Allium_ursinum.jpg/330px-387_Allium_ursinum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A387_Allium_ursinum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Illustration_Allium_ursinum1.jpg/500px-Illustration_Allium_ursinum1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Illustration